From 39ebc3818bb1ccd421440e113cca0cc59bfc299d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eicke Hecht <eicke.hecht@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:48:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] zynqmp-r5-echo: drop the loom packages from the lockfile

With loom gone from rustamp-metal (previous patch), the R5 example only
needs its aarch32 runtime crates from crates.io; the lockfile keeps
exactly those, so cargo resolves it --frozen against a vendored set.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [offline embedded build only; RustAmp
keeps loom for its model checks]
---
